The author thanks George Paras for technical review and for helpful signal-processing perspective
that informed the discussion of correlation, independence, and effective sample-size reasoning in
Section 2.1 and Appendix A.4.
A Derivation of the Statistical Horizon
The Statistical Horizon marks the model-based point at which the expected detector statistic
reaches a specified threshold in a finite text sample. The derivation starts from the canonical
green-list logit-biasing framework of Kirchenbauer et al. [1] and abstracts to a variance-normalized
detector-response parameter η.
5See Fed. R. Evid. 702; Daubert v. Merrell Dow Pharm., Inc., 509 U.S. 579 (1993); Frye v. United States, 293 F.
1013 (D.C. Cir. 1923).
