A.1 Preliminaries: Watermarking Generative Process
At each generation step t, the LLM produces logits ℓ
(t) ∈ R
|V |
. A secret pseudorandom function
(seeded by preceding tokens) partitions the vocabulary into a green list Gt of relative size γ ∈ (0, 1).
The watermarking rule adds a positive logit bias δ > 0 to green-list tokens. After softmax
normalization, the probability of sampling a green token rises from a baseline value p0 to a perturbed
value p1(δ). For small-to-moderate δ, the induced probability lift may be linearized: p1(δ) ≈ p0 + κδ,
where κ is a local response coefficient determined by the underlying token distribution and green-list
construction. Formally, κ = dp1/dδ|δ=0; in the idealized case where baseline green-token mass is
approximately γ, the local response is on the order of γ(1 − γ), so that smaller green-list fractions
and weaker biasing both reduce κ and thereby enlarge the required sample length through Equation
(1).
