A.4 Interpretive Limits
The derivation assumes a z-test-like detector, approximate token independence, and a locally linear
watermark response. A practically important point is the effect of dependence. Because green-list
assignment is seeded by preceding tokens and generated text is itself autocorrelated, exact token-level
independence is not expected in realistic samples. Under positive token-level correlation, the variance
of X exceeds the independence approximation, so the formula above tends to understate required
sample length. In that sense, the stylized derivation is plausibly optimistic: realistic dependence
would typically strengthen, not weaken, the paper’s cautionary conclusion.
